		<!-- Primary Meta Tags -->
		<title>Privacy Policy - Unslop Search</title>
		<meta name="title" content="Privacy Policy - Unslop Search" />
		<meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for Unslop Search. We don't collect data, track searches, or use analytics. Your preferences are stored locally on your device." />
		<link rel="canonical" href="https://unslopsearch.com/privacy/" />

		<!-- Open Graph -->
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:url" content="https://unslopsearch.com/privacy" />
		<meta property="og:title" content="Privacy Policy - Unslop Search" />
		<meta property="og:description" content="Privacy policy for the Unslop Search browser extension and website." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="container">
			<a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Unslop Search</a>

			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="last-updated">Last updated: January 23, 2026</p>

			<section>
				<h2>Overview</h2>
				<p>
					Unslop Search is committed to protecting your privacy. This extension is designed to enhance your search experience
					without compromising your personal data. We do not collect, store, or transmit any personal information.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Data Collection</h2>
				<p><strong>We do not collect any data.</strong></p>
				<p>The Unslop Search extension:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Does not collect your search queries</li>
					<li>Does not track your browsing history</li>
					<li>Does not collect personal information</li>
					<li>Does not use analytics or tracking services</li>
					<li>Does not transmit any data to external servers</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Local Storage</h2>
				<p>
					The extension stores your preferences (such as your preferred search engine and mode settings) locally
					on your device using Chrome's built-in storage API. This data:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Never leaves your device</li>
					<li>Is only used to remember your settings</li>
					<li>Can be cleared by uninstalling the extension</li>
					<li>Syncs across your Chrome browsers if you're signed into Chrome (via Chrome's sync feature, not our servers)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Permissions</h2>
				<p>The extension requires certain permissions to function:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Storage:</strong> To save your preferences locally</li>
					<li><strong>Web Navigation:</strong> To detect when you perform a search and apply AI-filtering parameters</li>
					<li><strong>Host Permissions:</strong> To modify search URLs on supported search engines (Google, DuckDuckGo, Brave Search)</li>
				</ul>
				<p>These permissions are used solely to provide the core functionality of filtering AI results from your searches.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
				<p>
					When you perform a search, you are redirected to your chosen search engine (Google, DuckDuckGo, Brave, etc.)
					with modified parameters. Your interaction with these search engines is governed by their respective privacy policies.
					We have no control over and assume no responsibility for the privacy practices of these third-party services.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Website</h2>
				<p>
					The unslopsearch.com website does not use cookies, analytics, or any tracking mechanisms.
					It is a static site that functions entirely in your browser.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this page
					with an updated "Last updated" date.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Contact</h2>
				<p>
					If you have any questions about this privacy policy, please contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@unslopsearch.com">privacy@unslopsearch.com</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>

